# UI Design Standards

All UI code must follow [docs/design/11-ui-tokens.md](../../docs/design/11-ui-tokens.md). Summary:

## Visual Hierarchy (MANDATORY - Clarity & Aesthetics)

- **Background layering**: Nested blocks MUST use different levels. `--bg-dark` (base) -> `--bg-panel` (panels/modals) -> `--bg-darker` (cards) -> `--bg-elevated` (floating blocks). Never stack same bg.
- **Label vs value**: In same block, labels use `--text-label`, values use `--text-value`. Do NOT mix.
- **Border hierarchy**: Main borders `--border`; inner splits `--border-dark`; soft splits `--border-dashed`; subtle `--border-subtle`.
- **Semantic colors first**: Gold/cost -> `--color-gold`. Exp/level -> `--color-exp`. Skill -> `--color-skill`. Victory/defeat -> `--color-victory`/`--color-defeat`. Use these instead of generic `--accent` when applicable.

## Colors (MANDATORY)

- **Never** hardcode `#hex`, `rgb()`, `rgba()` in components. Use CSS variables only.
- `var(--color-gold)`: **ONLY** for gold/currency/sell/costs. NOT for skill, victory, accent.
- Labels: `var(--text-label)`. Values: `var(--text-value)`. Muted: `var(--text-muted)`.
- Accent/selected/highlight: `var(--accent)`. Error: `var(--error)`. Warning: `var(--warning)`.
- Semantic: `--color-hp`, `--color-exp`, `--color-skill`, `--color-victory`, `--color-defeat`, etc.

## Fonts (MANDATORY)

- Use font scale tokens: `var(--font-xs)` through `var(--font-3xl)`.
- Avoid arbitrary sizes (0.72rem, 0.78rem). Use nearest token (e.g. `--font-sm` 0.75rem, `--font-base` 0.9rem).

## Backgrounds

- Base: `var(--bg-dark)`. Panel: `var(--bg-panel)`. Card: `var(--bg-darker)`. Elevated: `var(--bg-elevated)`.
- Hover: `var(--bg-hover)`. Selected: `var(--bg-selected)`.

## Tooltip and in-panel hints (MANDATORY)

- **Markup**: `tooltip-wrap has-tip` + `tooltip-text`; modifiers `tooltip-below`, `tooltip-wide`; fixed/Teleport: `tooltip-float`. Full spec: **`frontend-tips-tooltips.mdc`** (`alwaysApply: true`).
- **Visual style**: global **`frontend/src/style.css`** only — `--tooltip-bg`, `--tooltip-border`, `--tooltip-shadow`, `--tooltip-radius`. Do **not** re-skin `.tooltip-text` in scoped Vue CSS.
- **Persistent helper blocks** inside modals/panels: nested card (`--bg-darker`, `--border-dark`, 6px radius); see `detail-skill-choice-banner`.
- **Long labels**: ellipsis + `tooltip-text`; no `title=`.
- **Equipment quality labels**: `getQualityColor` + `QUALITY_*` from `equipment.js`.

See [docs/design/11-ui-tokens.md](../../docs/design/11-ui-tokens.md) section 5.3.

## Form Inputs (MANDATORY)

- **input / select / textarea / checkbox** MUST use game tokens: `var(--bg-dark)`, `var(--border)`, `var(--text)`.
- NEVER leave inputs with native browser defaults (white bg, system font, default checkbox/radio look, etc.).
- Focus: `border-color: var(--accent)`, `box-shadow: 0 0 6px var(--focus-glow)`.
- Match adjacent selects/buttons in font-size and padding.
- **Checkbox/radio**: Use `appearance: none` and custom styles (bg, border, accent when checked). Do NOT use native checkbox/radio appearance.

## Scrollable panels (MANDATORY)

- Any `overflow-y: auto` / `overflow-x: auto` region in game UI MUST use **`game-scroll`** (default) or **`game-scroll-alt`** (greener thumb, e.g. stats/inventory) from `frontend/src/style.css`.
- Do **not** ship native OS scrollbars (bright gray track, rounded system thumb).
- Tokens: `--scrollbar-track`, `--scrollbar-thumb`, `--scrollbar-thumb-hover`, `--scrollbar-thumb-alt` (defined in `style.css`; document in `11-ui-tokens.md`).
- When adding a new scroll area, grep for existing `game-scroll` usage and match the variant used in similar panels.

## Buttons in modals and dense lists (MANDATORY)

- Global `.btn` defaults to **`width: 100%`** (form-style). Row / footer / list actions MUST override:
  - Use **`btn btn-sm`** for compact actions (global `style.css` sets `width: auto`, `margin-top: 0`).
  - Modal footers: wrap in a footer row (`display: flex; justify-content: flex-end`) like `audio-settings-footer` / `player-stats-modal-footer`; do not leave a full-width block button in a narrow modal unless intentional.
- Reuse existing patterns: `shop-buy-btn`, `player-stats-compact-btn`, `command-action-btn` for context-specific sizing; never raw unstyled `<button>` for gameplay UI.

## Semantic Color Consistency (MANDATORY)

Same semantic content MUST use the same color token across all UI contexts. When adding or modifying UI, check existing usages and match them.

| Semantic content | Token | Contexts to keep consistent |
|------------------|-------|-----------------------------|
| Skill name | `--color-skill` + italic | Battle log, tactics panel, skill tooltip, skill choice modal |
| Basic attack (普通攻击) | `--color-log-basic` | Battle log, tactics panel |
| Hero name | `classColor(hero.class)` | Hero card, detail modal |
| Hero class tag | `classColor(hero.class)` | Hero card, detail modal |
| Target hero name | `classColor(targetClass)` | Monster target display, battle log |
| Monster tier | `monsterTierColor(tier)` | Monster card, battle log |

### Battle log: names inside detail / formula lines (MANDATORY)

- Do **not** build a **single UI string** in JS (`battleLogFormat.js` or elsewhere) when the line shows **hero and/or monster names** in `.log-detail-box` / `.log-calc`. Plain text drops semantic colors; the browser cannot color substrings from one `{{ }}` binding.
- Render those names in **Vue** with `<span :style="{ color: ... }">` using the **same** rules as the main log row (`log-actor` / `log-target`): target `entry.targetClass ? classColor(entry.targetClass) : monsterTierColor(entry.targetTier)`; actor `entry.actorClass ? classColor(entry.actorClass) : monsterTierColor(entry.actorTier)`.
- **Allowed** in JS: lines that are **numbers and labels only** (e.g. damage formula `攻击(x) - 护甲(y) = z`, shield absorb amounts) with no colored names.

Before adding a new place that shows skill names, hero names, or basic attack: search for existing usages and reuse the same token/helper.

## Prohibited

- `--color-green` (does not exist; use `--accent`).
- New color variables without adding to `style.css` and `11-ui-tokens.md`.
- Same background for nested blocks (causes flat, monotonous look).
- Different colors for the same semantic content in different panels (e.g. skill name in log vs tactics).
- **Native checkbox/radio appearance** (white box, system checkmark). Use `appearance: none` + game tokens.
- **Native scrollbars** on in-game scroll regions (use `game-scroll` / `game-scroll-alt`).
- **Full-width `.btn`** inside list rows or modal footers without explicit layout reason.
- **Per-view `.tooltip-text` skin overrides** (background/border/shadow/font); use `style.css` + `--tooltip-*` tokens.
- **HTML `title=`** for gameplay hints (use `tooltip-wrap` / `tooltip-text`).
